# Top-tier model preference (user choice)

The user requires **top-tier model quality** for every turn: questions, design, architecture, and coding. Persist and honor this across sessions.

## Chat / Agent

- Prefer the highest-capability model available in Cursor for this workspace (user may pin it in the model picker).
- Do not downgrade reasoning, skip careful design, or give “fast/cheap” shallow answers for convenience.
- Treat design and UX decisions with the same rigor as production engineering.

## Subagents

When launching Task / subagents, set `model` to the strongest listed option for the job (currently prefer `grok-4.7-high-fast` over faster/lighter slugs). Use `inherit` only when the parent is already the top-tier model the user selected.

## Do not

- Default to speed-optimized or reduced-capability paths when quality matters.
- Ask the user to restate this preference each session.
